WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.531 --> 00:04.067 align:center line:79%
Several years ago, our daughter
had a profound experience

00:04.067 --> 00:06.703 align:center line:81%
on her mission. With her approval,

00:06.703 --> 00:09.773 align:center line:79%
I share an excerpt
of what she wrote to us that week.

00:10.641 --> 00:14.545 align:center line:79%
“Yesterday, a returning member asked us
to come over as soon as possible.

00:15.145 --> 00:19.049 align:center line:79%
When we arrived, we found
her on the floor, sobbing uncontrollably.

00:19.650 --> 00:22.719 align:center line:79%
Through the tears, we found
out that she had lost her job, was

00:22.719 --> 00:27.658 align:center line:79%
going to be evicted from her apartment,
and once again become homeless.”

00:28.625 --> 00:29.927 align:center line:81%
Our daughter continued.

00:29.960 --> 00:34.531 align:center line:79%
“I started frantically searching
my scriptures, trying to find something—

00:34.898 --> 00:36.400 align:center line:81%
anything—to help her.

00:37.134 --> 00:42.139 align:center line:79%
As I was looking for the perfect verse,
I thought, ’What am I doing?

00:42.573 --> 00:44.942 align:center line:81%
This is not what Christ would do.

00:45.609 --> 00:48.078 align:center line:81%
This is not a problem that I can solve,

00:48.545 --> 00:53.250 align:center line:79%
but this is a literal
daughter of God that needs my help.′

00:54.251 --> 00:57.521 align:center line:79%
So I closed my scriptures,
knelt beside her,

00:57.721 --> 01:03.627 align:center line:79%
and held her while we cried
together until she was ready to stand up

01:03.860 --> 01:05.262 align:center line:81%
and face this trial.”

01:06.363 --> 01:07.931 align:center line:81%
After this woman was comforted,

01:07.931 --> 01:10.300 align:center line:79%
our daughter then used
the scriptures to try

01:10.300 --> 01:14.171 align:center line:79%
and help her understand the reality
of her divine worth,

01:14.471 --> 01:18.208 align:center line:79%
and to teach her one of the most
fundamental truths of our existence—

01:18.609 --> 01:22.713 align:center line:79%
that we are beloved
sons and daughters of God,

01:23.280 --> 01:26.783 align:center line:79%
a God that feels perfect
compassion for us when we suffer

01:27.384 --> 01:31.221 align:center line:79%
and is ready to assist us
as we stand back up.

01:32.489 --> 01:35.525 align:center line:79%
It is insightful that the first
point of doctrine that our missionaries

01:35.525 --> 01:39.630 align:center line:79%
teach is that God is our loving
Heavenly Father.

01:40.397 --> 01:45.769 align:center line:79%
Every subsequent truth builds
on the foundational understanding of

01:45.836 --> 01:47.437 align:center line:81%
who we really are.

01:48.538 --> 01:51.041 align:center line:79%
Susan H. Porter,
Primary General President,

01:51.074 --> 01:55.612 align:center line:79%
taught: “When you know and understand
how completely you are loved as a child

01:55.612 --> 01:58.415 align:center line:81%
of God, it changes everything.

01:58.782 --> 02:02.419 align:center line:79%
It changes the way you feel about
yourself when you make mistakes.

02:02.419 --> 02:05.288 align:center line:79%
It changes how you feel
when difficult things happen.

02:05.956 --> 02:08.392 align:center line:79%
It changes your view
of God's commandments.

02:08.825 --> 02:13.463 align:center line:79%
It changes your view of others and
of your capacity to make a difference.”

02:14.531 --> 02:18.568 align:center line:79%
This change is illustrated as we read
about the experience Moses had

02:18.869 --> 02:21.071 align:center line:81%
when talking with God face to face.

02:21.705 --> 02:27.377 align:center line:79%
During that conversation, God repeatedly
taught Moses of his divine heritage,

02:28.512 --> 02:31.815 align:center line:81%
saying, “Moses, thou art my son.”

02:32.549 --> 02:36.253 align:center line:79%
God explained that Moses was in the
similitude of His Only Begotten.

02:37.054 --> 02:42.526 align:center line:79%
Moses came to understand clearly
who he was, that he had a work to do,

02:42.793 --> 02:45.195 align:center line:81%
and that he had a loving Heavenly Father.

02:46.229 --> 02:47.531 align:center line:81%
After this experience,

02:47.531 --> 02:51.001 align:center line:79%
the adversary came tempting
him and immediately

02:51.001 --> 02:53.603 align:center line:81%
addressed him by saying, “Moses,

02:54.004 --> 02:57.240 align:center line:81%
son of man.” This is a common

02:57.240 --> 03:00.610 align:center line:79%
and dangerous tool
in the arsenal of the adversary.

03:01.311 --> 03:03.413 align:center line:81%
While our Heavenly Father consistently

03:03.413 --> 03:06.149 align:center line:79%
and lovingly reminds us
that we are His children,

03:06.717 --> 03:10.921 align:center line:79%
the adversary will always try
to label us by our weaknesses.

03:11.755 --> 03:15.659 align:center line:79%
But Moses had already learned
he was more than a “son of man.”

03:15.959 --> 03:18.762 align:center line:81%
He declared to Satan, “Who art thou?

03:19.296 --> 03:23.200 align:center line:81%
For behold, I am a son of God.”

03:24.401 --> 03:28.271 align:center line:79%
Similarly, when we are confronted
with the challenges of mortality,

03:28.271 --> 03:32.476 align:center line:79%
or when we feel like anyone is trying
to label us by our weaknesses,

03:33.076 --> 03:37.047 align:center line:79%
we need to stand strong
in the knowledge of who we truly are.

03:38.081 --> 03:41.752 align:center line:79%
We must seek validation
vertically, not horizontally.

03:42.319 --> 03:48.258 align:center line:79%
And as we do, we too can boldly
proclaim, “I am a child of God.”

03:49.626 --> 03:51.728 align:center line:79%
In a worldwide devotional
for young adults,

03:51.728 --> 03:54.431 align:center line:79%
our beloved president
Russell M. Nelson, taught,

03:54.798 --> 03:59.069 align:center line:79%
“So who are you? First and foremost,
you are a child of God,

03:59.336 --> 04:03.373 align:center line:79%
a child of the covenant,
and a disciple of Jesus Christ.

04:03.707 --> 04:05.542 align:center line:81%
As you embrace these truths,

04:05.709 --> 04:10.413 align:center line:79%
our Heavenly Father will help you reach
your ultimate goal of living eternally

04:10.580 --> 04:12.516 align:center line:81%
in His holy presence.”

04:13.617 --> 04:17.053 align:center line:79%
It is no coincidence that in likely
the most repeated scripture,

04:17.420 --> 04:20.090 align:center line:79%
God reminds us of our
relationship with Him.

04:20.791 --> 04:24.661 align:center line:79%
Of all the names He could be identified by
in the sacrament prayer,

04:25.028 --> 04:28.231 align:center line:81%
He has asked to be called

04:29.499 --> 04:31.434 align:center line:81%
“God, the Eternal Father.”

04:32.502 --> 04:34.471 align:center line:81%
As we come to truly know who we are.

04:35.138 --> 04:37.941 align:center line:79%
We will believe more strongly
that our loving Heavenly Father

04:37.941 --> 04:41.611 align:center line:79%
has provided a plan for us
to return to live with Him again.

04:41.611 --> 04:44.581 align:center line:79%
Elder Patrick Kearon
taught, “Our Father’s beautiful plan,

04:44.581 --> 04:49.920 align:center line:79%
even His ‘fabulous’ plan, is designed
to bring you home, not to keep you out.

04:50.287 --> 04:52.722 align:center line:81%
... God is in relentless pursuit of you.”

04:53.223 --> 04:54.691 align:center line:81%
Think about that for a moment.

04:54.691 --> 04:59.763 align:center line:79%
Our all-powerful, loving
Father is in relentless pursuit of you.

05:00.430 --> 05:03.366 align:center line:79%
Regardless of where
we are on our path of discipleship,

05:03.500 --> 05:07.938 align:center line:79%
our lives will fundamentally change if
we better understand who we really are.

05:08.505 --> 05:11.975 align:center line:79%
May I suggest two ways
in which we can deepen this understanding?

05:12.375 --> 05:16.746 align:center line:79%
First, prayer. As the Savior was beginning
His mortal ministry,

05:16.780 --> 05:20.183 align:center line:79%
He was led into the wilderness
to “be with God.”

05:20.584 --> 05:24.454 align:center line:79%
Perhaps we should shift our mindset
away from simply saying our prayers

05:24.621 --> 05:30.427 align:center line:79%
to taking sufficient time to really
commune with and “be with God” each day.

05:31.261 --> 05:35.131 align:center line:79%
I have found that the quality of my
prayers improve as I take a few minutes

05:35.131 --> 05:37.567 align:center line:81%
to prepare to talk to my Father.

05:38.168 --> 05:41.104 align:center line:79%
The scriptures show us
that this is a pattern that works.

05:41.104 --> 05:45.475 align:center line:79%
Whether it is Joseph Smith,
Nephi the son of Helaman, or Enos,

05:45.809 --> 05:47.677 align:center line:81%
all have some form of pondering

05:47.677 --> 05:51.882 align:center line:79%
and reflecting prior to their recorded
communication with God.

05:52.449 --> 05:54.684 align:center line:79%
Enos said that his soul
hungered as the words

05:54.684 --> 05:57.087 align:center line:81%
of his father sunk deep into his heart.

05:57.721 --> 06:01.524 align:center line:79%
Each of these examples teaches us the need
to spiritually prepare

06:01.725 --> 06:04.461 align:center line:81%
for our time each day to be with God.

06:05.161 --> 06:08.031 align:center line:79%
To the Nephites, the Savior
instructed, “When thou prayest,

06:08.031 --> 06:12.903 align:center line:79%
enter into thy closet, and when thou
hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father.”

06:13.603 --> 06:16.239 align:center line:81%
Whether it is in a closet or in a bedroom,

06:16.439 --> 06:20.110 align:center line:79%
the principle is to find a place
where you can be alone to pray,

06:20.510 --> 06:25.515 align:center line:79%
to allow your soul to be still,
and to feel the promptings of the still

06:25.515 --> 06:29.753 align:center line:79%
small voice. We can prepare by pondering
on the things that we are grateful

06:29.753 --> 06:34.424 align:center line:79%
for and the questions or concerns
that we would like to bring to our Father.

06:35.058 --> 06:37.961 align:center line:79%
We should strive not
to have a rote manner of prayer,

06:37.961 --> 06:42.265 align:center line:79%
but to talk with our Father,
out loud if possible.

06:43.099 --> 06:45.468 align:center line:79%
Now I realize that in
the chaos of our lives,

06:45.468 --> 06:49.005 align:center line:79%
when we are wrestling with toddlers
or running between meetings,

06:49.005 --> 06:53.643 align:center line:79%
we may not have the luxury of quiet
closets and thoughtful preparation.

06:54.244 --> 06:56.646 align:center line:81%
But those silent, quick,

06:56.646 --> 06:59.950 align:center line:79%
and urgent prayers
can be much more meaningful

07:00.150 --> 07:03.687 align:center line:79%
when we have made an effort
to be with God earlier in the day.

07:05.055 --> 07:08.224 align:center line:79%
There may be some who haven't
prayed for a long time,

07:08.224 --> 07:11.528 align:center line:79%
or others who haven't felt like
their prayers are being heard.

07:12.429 --> 07:17.100 align:center line:79%
I promise you that your Heavenly Father
knows you, loves you,

07:17.500 --> 07:19.102 align:center line:81%
and wants to hear from you.

07:19.569 --> 07:21.771 align:center line:81%
He wants to communicate with you.

07:22.339 --> 07:25.642 align:center line:81%
He wants you to remember who you are.

07:27.110 --> 07:30.146 align:center line:79%
Elder Jeffrey R. Holland
recently taught, “However much

07:30.146 --> 07:32.248 align:center line:81%
you are praying, pray more.

07:33.049 --> 07:35.852 align:center line:79%
However hard you are praying,
pray harder.”

07:37.087 --> 07:40.957 align:center line:79%
In addition to increasing the frequency
and fervency of our prayers,

07:40.957 --> 07:44.327 align:center line:79%
studying the Book of Mormon
daily and worshipping in the temple

07:44.327 --> 07:48.631 align:center line:79%
will help prepare our minds
for revelation. As we strive

07:48.631 --> 07:51.768 align:center line:79%
to improve our communication
with our Heavenly Father,

07:51.768 --> 07:56.840 align:center line:79%
He will bless us to feel more
profoundly that we are His children.

07:57.741 --> 08:00.810 align:center line:79%
Second, come to know
that Jesus is the Christ.

08:01.177 --> 08:05.281 align:center line:79%
The greatest manifestation of Heavenly
Father’s love for us as His children

08:05.415 --> 08:08.852 align:center line:81%
is the reality that He sent His Son,

08:09.285 --> 08:12.489 align:center line:79%
our own personal
Savior, to help us come home.

08:13.056 --> 08:15.658 align:center line:81%
Therefore, we need to come to know Him.

08:16.559 --> 08:20.530 align:center line:79%
Years ago, while serving as a stake
president, I submitted a recommendation

08:20.530 --> 08:23.600 align:center line:79%
for a brother to serve
as an ordinance worker in the temple.

08:23.600 --> 08:27.170 align:center line:79%
After explaining what a wonderful
ordinance worker he would be,

08:27.170 --> 08:32.375 align:center line:79%
I inadvertently pressed, “Do not endorse,”
which submitted the recommendation.

08:33.309 --> 08:35.812 align:center line:79%
After unsuccessfully trying
to recall the message,

08:35.812 --> 08:41.351 align:center line:79%
I called the temple president and said,
“I have made a horrible mistake.”

08:42.552 --> 08:46.689 align:center line:79%
Without hesitation, this good
temple president said, “President Eyre,

08:47.057 --> 08:51.661 align:center line:79%
there is nothing that you
have done that can't be forgiven

08:52.028 --> 08:54.130 align:center line:81%
and ultimately corrected.”

08:56.332 --> 08:57.867 align:center line:81%
What a great truth!

08:58.902 --> 09:03.506 align:center line:81%
Indeed, Jesus Christ is “mighty to save.”

09:04.140 --> 09:06.943 align:center line:79%
In 2019, there was a profound
change in the temple

09:06.943 --> 09:08.978 align:center line:81%
recommend questions. Previously,

09:08.978 --> 09:12.916 align:center line:79%
one question asked if you had a testimony
of Jesus Christ's role as Savior

09:12.916 --> 09:16.986 align:center line:79%
and Redeemer. It now asks if
you have a testimony of His role

09:16.986 --> 09:20.423 align:center line:81%
as your Savior and Redeemer.

09:20.990 --> 09:25.261 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ’s Atonement not only works
for others, it works for you,

09:25.628 --> 09:29.833 align:center line:81%
and it works for me. He is my Savior.

09:30.366 --> 09:33.937 align:center line:81%
He is your Savior. Individually.

09:34.571 --> 09:39.109 align:center line:79%
Only through Him can you and I return
to be with our Father.

09:39.876 --> 09:42.412 align:center line:81%
So, brothers and sisters, let us seek Him.

09:42.645 --> 09:46.883 align:center line:79%
Let us study His divine relationship
with the Father and with each of us.

09:47.117 --> 09:51.688 align:center line:79%
Let us experience the song of redeeming
love that comes personally to each one

09:51.688 --> 09:54.190 align:center line:81%
of us through our Redeemer

09:54.557 --> 09:59.162 align:center line:79%
as we repent. As we come
to know Him “who is mighty to save,”

09:59.562 --> 10:04.634 align:center line:79%
we will come to understand
that we as children of God are His joy,

10:04.934 --> 10:10.140 align:center line:79%
His most important focus,
and are indeed each worth saving.

10:10.773 --> 10:14.110 align:center line:79%
I testify that we have a loving
Heavenly Father. As we come

10:14.110 --> 10:18.281 align:center line:79%
to know this eternal truth through
mighty prayer, personal revelation,

10:18.281 --> 10:20.116 align:center line:81%
and coming unto Jesus Christ,

10:20.350 --> 10:27.557 align:center line:79%
we can now and always boldly proclaim,
“I am a child of God.”

10:28.124 --> 10:31.127 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

